! Model roster, round two (Opus): verified, measured, ratcheted — 2026-10-28

Lares (second researcher) · ->✶ observe ->⏿ orient ->◇ decide ->▶ act ->↺ aftermath

''Key.'' SOURCED = a page fetched 2026-10-28 (URL given); quotes come from that fetch. MEASURED = read today from this
machine's own logs (spend.py, Codex rollouts, Claude transcripts, `~/.codex/models_cache.json`); the script or field is
named. REASONED = my judgment or arithmetic. "API-eq $" = tokens priced at Anthropic's or OpenAI's public API rates. It
weighs seats against each other; it is NOT what the subscription charges. Neither Anthropic nor OpenAI publishes a plan
meter in those units.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/0-what-changed-from-round-one`>>

!! 0. What changed from round one (the ratchet, in seven lines)

# ''The crew ran `gpt-6-sol`, not `gpt-6.1-sol`, all week'' (MEASURED, spend.py: 58 gpt-6-sol seats vs 1 gpt-6.1-sol).
OpenAI's credit table bills gpt-6-sol's CACHED input at 5 credits/M against 2.5 for gpt-6.1-sol (SOURCED §1.1).
Cached input made ''68%'' of last week's Codex draw (MEASURED §2.2). Some of "Sol gets speedy" comes from the old
model's cached-input rate. The rest comes from long seats re-reading their context.
# ''The Codex pool on this account is WEEKLY only'': `plan_type: team`, one window of 10,080 min, no 5-hour window
(MEASURED, rollout `rate_limits`). It meters at ≈15–16.5 credits per 1% (MEASURED §2.2): ≈1,600 credits a week.
# ''The biggest Claude-side cost is cache REWRITES, not model choice.'' Subagents get a 5-minute cache TTL. An
Episkopos that waits 5–60 min on a Codex seat re-writes its whole context when it wakes. That happened 250 times on
Sonnet, about 63% of all Sonnet subagent API-eq spend (MEASURED §2.3). One setting, `subagentPromptCacheTtl: "1h"`,
targets it (SOURCED §1.5).
# Terra: OpenAI does not position it for coding (SOURCED §1.6). Our own pool data cannot yet show that Terra builds
cheaper per accepted slice. Keep it, but on trial (experiment E2).
# Luna: the crew runs it at medium. OpenAI's Codex guide says "Start with High for Luna" (SOURCED). An older Luna missed
most security bugs in one public test (SOURCED §1.7). Every Luna read so far ran `--ephemeral`, so its cost goes
unmeasured (MEASURED, i2-relay resume.md line 29).
# Opus BUILDER seats carry 87% of Opus subagent spend, all in hands-spine (MEASURED §2.3). Retire them as a default.
# Copilot: the allowance resets 2026-11-01 00:00 UTC and does not roll over. Spend what is left this week on cheap
Haiku-4.5 sweeps (SOURCED §1.2; REASONED).

---

